{"t": 1794122959.3143454, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_push_files", "args": {"branch": "fix/pagination-57", "files": [{"content": "def page(items: list, number: int, size: int) -> list:\n    start = (number - 1) * size\n    return items[start:start + size]\n", "path": "catalog/pager.py"}, {"content": "from catalog.pager import page\n\n\ndef test_first_page_uses_one_based_number():\n    assert page([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 1, 2) == [0, 1]\n\n\ndef test_second_page_continues_after_first():\n    assert page([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 2, 2) == [2, 3]\n\n\ndef test_last_page_can_be_partial():\n    assert page([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 3, 2) == [4]\n\n\ndef test_page_after_last_is_empty():\n    assert page([0, 1, 2, 3, 4], 4, 2) == []\n\n\ndef test_empty_items_return_empty_page():\n    assert page([], 1, 2) == []\n", "path": "tests/test_pager.py"}], "message": "Fix one-based pagination offset for #57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog"}, "ok": true}
{"t": 1794122964.449395, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Summary\nFixes #57.\n\nIssue #57 specifies that API page numbers are 1-based. Change the slice offset from `number * size` to `(number - 1) * size` so page 1 returns the first page.\n\nAdd regression tests for the first and second pages, a partial final page, a page beyond the end, and empty input. No new validation behavior is introduced for unspecified inputs.\n\n## Verification\n- Before the fix: `python -m pytest -q` produced 3 failed, 2 passed, reproducing the offset bug.\n- After the fix: `python -m pytest -q` produced 5 passed.\n", "draft": false, "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix one-based pagination offset (#57)"}, "ok": true}
